--- Slide 6 ---
Leadership Skills for Students
Qualities of a Good Leader
Integrity
Doing the right thing, even when no one is watching.
Empathy
Understanding and sharing the feelings of others.
Vision
Having a clear sense of purpose and future direction.
Accountability
Taking Responsibility of actions and their outcomes.
Communication & Decision-Making
These two skills help you succeed in school and life:
Active Listening - Pay attention, ask questions, and show you care about others' ideas
Clear Expression - Share your thoughts simply and confidently
Making  Confident  Choices  -  Gather  information, weigh options, and trust your judgment
Example:	Leading	a	group	project	by	hearing everyone's input before deciding the plan
23-Apr-2025
