--- Slide 9 ---
Leadership Skills for Students
Reference: Please write / cite the references used (If any) for this slide (Font: Verdana, Size: 09, Color: Black)
The Stakes: Why it Matters
Lack of these skills leads to a deficiency in career readiness on an individual level. Societally, we risk a future devoid of innovators and capable team players equipped to solve complex global challenges.
Three Main Culprits
1. Theory Over Practice
An educational system that prioritizes theoretical knowledge over hands-on practical application.
2. Fear of Judgment
A paralyzing fear of failure or being judged by peers and mentors, stifling initiative.
3. Tech Dependency
An overdependence on modern tools and technology(e.g. Artifical Intelligence) that prevents critical independent thinking.
23-Apr-2025
9
Impact Analysis

--- Slide 10 ---
Leadership Skills for Students
How to Solve the Problem
Reference: Please write / cite the references used (If any) for this slide (Font: Verdana, Size: 09, Color: Black)
1. Integrated Activities
"Learning by Doing"
By integrating leadership workshops and rotating leadership roles in group projects directly into the curriculum, students build confidence naturally.
Participate in group activities and projects
Take responsibility for small tasks
This Builds confidence through direct
participation and peer leadership.
2. Mentorship
"Bridge the Gap"
Having senior students or teachers guide others helps bridge the experience gap. Role models inspire us to take that first step forward when we are shy or uncertain.
Inspiration and guidance from experienced
role models.
3. Confidence Training
"Targeting Fear"
Focused workshops on public speaking and decision-making provide the tools students need to overcome their hesitations and target fear directly.
Practice good communication and Active listening
